## DEFINITION
PyMOL is a molecular visualization software used to view, analyze, and create high-quality 3D images of proteins, nucleic acids, and other biomolecules.

## PURPOSE
- Visualize 3D molecular structures.
- Analyze protein and ligand interactions.
- Create publication-quality molecular images.
- Study structural features of biomolecules.

## APPLICATIONS
- Protein structure visualization.
- Drug and ligand binding analysis.
- Structural biology research.
- Molecular modeling and education.

## COMMON FEATURES
- Interactive 3D visualization.
- Multiple molecular display styles (cartoon, surface, sticks, spheres).
- Structure measurement and labeling.
- Image rendering and animation.

## FILES TO UPLOAD
- PDB (.pdb)
- mmCIF (.cif)
- MOL2 (.mol2)
- SDF (.sdf)

## IMPORTANT POINTS
- Widely used in structural biology and bioinformatics.
- Produces high-quality publication-ready images.
- Supports scripting for automation.
- Compatible with multiple molecular structure formats.
